# HPACK's Huffman code (RFC 7541 § 5.2 and Appendix B): a string's bytes
# written in the code and read back. The tables below are the appendix's,
# read from the RFC's text; the code is canonical (the codes of one length
# are consecutive, taken in the order of their symbols), so reading walks
# the lengths and needs no tree.

